  "configuration_id": "config_030",
  "reason": "Evidence: All 5 completed experiments used singleprofile. The best config (config_028: scvi_n200 + resnet50 + concat) achieves 0.536 acc / 0.516 F1, confirming scvi_n200 as the superior RNA encoder and that multimodal fusion with resnet50 adds value. However, the multiprofile axis (with aggregation over multiple cellular profiles) is entirely unexplored, representing a major source of uncertainty about whether richer cellular representations can push performance further. Question: config_030 (scvi_n200 + resnet50 + avgpool + concat, multiprofile) is the minimal, direct extension of config_028—same encoders, same fusion—changing only the profile representation from single to multiple with average-pool aggregation. This cleanly isolates the effect of multiprofile aggregation. Why this is the best next experiment: It tests the single largest unexplored design axis while holding all other variables at their best-known settings. If multiprofile+avgpool improves on 0.536, it opens a productive direction (then test transformer aggregation, ViT-L, weighted fusion). If it does not, we gain strong evidence that singleprofile suffices, saving budget from exploring 20+ multiprofile variants. Under a limited budget, resolving this binary question is more informative than, e.g., testing weighted fusion (a smaller expected delta) or a new image encoder (a secondary axis given image-only performance was very weak at 0.208)."
}

